Exercise: sa-systemd-review (chapter 9 lab)

Work on servera, with sudo or as root.

A custom service
 1. /usr/local/bin/reporter.sh, an executable script (mode 755) that
    appends a line with the time and the text "reporter alive" to
    /var/log/reporter.log every ${INTERVAL:-10} seconds.
 2. /etc/systemd/system/reporter.service that runs the script with
    ExecStart, restarts it on failure, and is wanted by
    multi-user.target.
 3. A drop-in /etc/systemd/system/reporter.service.d/10-interval.conf that
    sets Environment=INTERVAL=2. Do not edit the unit file for this.
 4. The service is running now and enabled at boot, and has written to its
    log.

Service policy
 5. bluetooth.service is masked.
 6. mdmonitor.service is stopped and disabled.

Boot
 7. The default target is multi-user.target.

Then, on workstation:  lab grade sa-systemd-review
